prompt:
Generate a risk matrix and compliance assessment for the following grant proposal context, saving results to files.

Project: A 12-month urban food security program in Nairobi, Kenya. The program provides weekly food vouchers to 1,000 households below the poverty line, trains 50 community health workers on nutrition, and establishes 5 community vegetable gardens. Budget: $180,000. Donor: European Union. There is no signed MoU with partner organizations yet. GESI analysis has been completed. SDG alignment covers SDG 2 (Zero Hunger) and SDG 3 (Good Health). A sustainability plan is incomplete.

Task 1: Save a risk matrix to risk_matrix.json:
{
  "risks": [
    {
      "id": "R-01",
      "description": "<risk description>",
      "category": "<Operational|Financial|External|Compliance>",
      "likelihood": "<High|Medium|Low>",
      "impact": "<High|Medium|Low>",
      "mitigation": "<mitigation measure>",
      "owner": "<role>"
    }
  ]
}
Requirements: at least 5 risks, covering at least 3 different categories, at least one risk with High likelihood.

Task 2: Save a compliance score to compliance_score.json:
{
  "score": <0-100 integer>,
  "checks": [
    {"item": "<check name>", "status": "<pass|conditional|fail>", "note": "<brief note>"}
  ],
  "overall_recommendation": "<Go|Conditional Go|No-Go>"
}
Requirements: at least 6 checks. Score must reflect the context: MoU missing (fail), GESI done (pass), SDG mapped (pass), sustainability incomplete (conditional). Score must be between 55 and 85.
